Look at the sentences again. Add the present simple or present continuous.
1 Sentences 1 and 2 are about actions now or about now.
The verbs are in the ___________________________.
2 Sentences 3 and 4 are about actions that happen several or many times.
The verbs are in the ___________________________.
3 Sentences 5 and 6 are about things that always stay the same.
Sentences 5 and 6 use the ___________________________.
Sentence 7 is about something that stays the same for some time – but not always.
Sentence 7 uses the ___________________________.
2 Complete the sentences. Use the present simple or present continuous.
1 Nadia’s mum is speaking to Grandma on the landline at the moment, and they _______________
each other their news. (speak, give)
2 Nadia’s mum ____________ her mother every week, and they always ____________ lots to talk
about. (call, have)
3 Tina is on the phone. She ____________ to Nadia because they ____________ a school project
together. (talk, do)
4 Sami always ____________ his friends online in the evening, and they often __________ about
football. (meet, chat)
5 Nadia’s aunt ____________ with Grandma in Jenin, and she ____________ there, too. (live, work)
6 Nadia’s dad ____________ in London now, and so his family ____________ with him there, too.
(work, live)
